  "title": "He Wanted CC'd On Everything. I CC'd Him On Everything.",
  "script": "CC him on everything? My new regional manager announced that every email, no matter how small, needed him CC'd\u2014no exceptions, so he could stay in the loop. I complied. I CC'd him on lunch orders. I CC'd him when the printer jammed. I even CC'd him on a reply-all thanking someone for coffee. Within four days, his inbox had over eleven hundred unread messages, and he missed the actual urgent email about a shipment delay, buried under three hundred about bagels. I hope he liked bagels. He called an emergency meeting to demand better judgment about what counted as necessary. I quoted his no-exceptions policy in front of everyone. He changed the policy within the hour. Funny how fast judgment returns when the inbox revolt reaches its author. He wanted every email\u2014still?",
